; One variable: the exposures, 2 and 1, of two SubViewports that share the 2D canvas's World3D and
; its sky. Godot bakes the one radiance in the first render, ViewA's, as children render first
; (`renderer_viewport.cpp:91-127`, `sky.cpp:1263-1369`), and each view draws its background at its own
; exposure. No other scene draws one sky at two exposures, so none shows a regression in it.

